{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-glossary-rigid-category","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:glossary-rigid-category","kind":"remark","title":"Rigid category","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-glossary-left-dual","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-glossary-right-dual"],"tags":["glossary","category-theory","monoidal","duality"],"defines":["rigid-category"],"text":"glossary-rigid-category.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"rem:glossary-rigid-category\"></a>\n<strong>Remark.</strong> <em>Rigid category</em></p>\n<p><strong><dfn class=\"defterm\" id=\"term-rigid-category\">Rigid category</dfn>.</strong> A monoidal category in which every object has both a left dual and a right dual.</p>\n<p><strong>Mathlib reference.</strong>\n<code>CategoryTheory.RigidCategory</code> (class).\nImport: <code>Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Rigid.Basic</code>.</p>\n"}
